---
import PageHero from "../components/PageHero.astro";
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base title="Terms" description="The terms for using Roomwave as a presenter or as part of an audience." path="/terms">
  <PageHero eyebrow="Terms" title="The terms, in plain words." lead="Last updated 15 October 2026." />
  <section class="section-tight">
    <div class="container prose">
      <h2>Using Roomwave</h2>
      <p>
        Roomwave lets presenters ask questions that an audience answers on their phones. By creating an account or joining a session you agree to these terms. If you use Roomwave
        for an organisation, you agree to them on its behalf.
      </p>

      <h2>Your content</h2>
      <p>
        Presentations, questions and answers belong to the people who wrote them. You give us permission to store and show them only so that Roomwave can work: to put them on the
        screen, on phones and in your results.
      </p>

      <h2>Fair use</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Do not use Roomwave to harass, threaten or deceive anyone, or to collect information people have not agreed to give.</li>
        <li>Do not try to break, overload or get around the limits of the service.</li>
        <li>Presenters are responsible for the sessions they run and for moderating them.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>We may suspend an account or end a session that breaks these rules. We will tell you why unless the law prevents it.</p>

      <h2>Plans and payment</h2>
      <p>
        Free stays free within its limits. Paid plans are billed by invoice in Kenyan shillings, for the period shown on the invoice. A Pro trial lasts 14 days and ends by itself;
        nothing is charged unless you ask us to invoice you.
      </p>

      <h2>Availability</h2>
      <p>
        We work hard to keep Roomwave running, especially during live sessions, but we cannot promise it will never be interrupted. Answers already saved are kept if a connection
        drops.
      </p>

      <h2>Liability</h2>
      <p>
        Roomwave is provided as it is. As far as the law allows, we are not liable for indirect losses, and our total liability is limited to what you paid us in the twelve months
        before the claim.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes and the law</h2>
      <p>
        We may update these terms, and we will tell account holders about important changes by email before they apply. These terms are governed by the laws of Kenya.
      </p>
      <p>Questions about them? Write to us from the <a href="/contact">contact page</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
